The rule for recover_json_object says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. For the input fence[ S A ] A, the fence holds S and A, so the last object inside the fence is A. For the rewritten text fence[ S A ] A A, the fence still holds S and A, and the last object inside the fence remains A. Therefore the recovery kernel should be unchanged between the two texts.